  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Missouri received $10.2B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The state recorded 104,832 contract awards, with an average award size of $96.9K. Obligations fell 27.3% year over year. Fiscal-year histories show variation: FY21 totaled $13.3B, FY22 totaled $11.2B, FY23 totaled $15.6B, FY24 totaled $16.2B, and FY25 totaled $14B. The Department of Defense led buying activity with $6.9B, followed by the Department of Energy with $2.1B. THE BOEING COMPANY received $4.4B, and HONEYWELL FEDERAL MANUFACTURING & TECHNOLOGIES, LLC received $2.1B. Aircraft Manufacturing is the largest industry by obligations at $3.1B, and Facilities Support Services follows with $2.2B. The data cover contract obligations and represent fiscal-year-to-date totals, not full-year results. Use the figures above when planning capture strategies or reviewing market concentration, because buying is concentrated in a few agencies, vendors, and industries.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has federal contracting trended in Missouri?",
        "body": "FY2026 to date obligations stand at $10.2B. Fiscal-year totals were $13.3B in FY21, $11.2B in FY22, $15.6B in FY23, $16.2B in FY24, and $14B in FY25. Obligations fell 27.3% year over year. Award activity totaled 104,832 awards with an average award size of $96.9K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which sectors and vendors dominate Missouri contracting?",
        "body": "Aircraft Manufacturing leads industries with $3.1B in obligations, and Facilities Support Services follows with $2.2B. THE BOEING COMPANY is the largest vendor with $4.4B, and HONEYWELL FEDERAL MANUFACTURING & TECHNOLOGIES, LLC is second with $2.1B. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer at $6.9B, and the Department of Energy is next at $2.1B."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to Missouri?",
      "a": "The state of Missouri received $10.2B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The total number of awards was 104,832 and the average award size was $96.9K. Obligations fell 27.3% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations were $13.3B in FY21, $11.2B in FY22, $15.6B in FY23, $16.2B in FY24, and $14B in FY25."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies award the most contracts in Missouri?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $6.9B in FY2026 to date. The Department of Energy obligated $2.1B, and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $399M. Other top buyers include the Department of Agriculture at $221M and the Department of Veterans Affairs at $217M."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are the largest federal contractors in Missouri?",
      "a": "THE BOEING COMPANY is the largest federal contractor in Missouri, receiving $4.4B in FY2026 to date. HONEYWELL FEDERAL MANUFACTURING & TECHNOLOGIES, LLC received $2.1B, and THE BOEING COMPANY also appears with $692M in another line. EVERNORTH FEDERAL SERVICES INC received $687M and EASTERN AIR EXPRESS LLC received $216M."
